# Backend Layered Architecture (Mandatory)

Before implementing, modifying, or reviewing **any** Java under `senior-post-api`, you **must** read and follow:

`.cursor/skills/backend-foundation-capabilities/SKILL.md` — especially **§10 Layered Architecture**、**§11 Comments & Logging**，以及 **Mandatory Rules**。

## Hard requirement

All database access follows this chain only:

```
Controller → Business Service → IService / ServiceImpl → Mapper → Table
```

## Never

- Inject or call `Mapper` from **Controller** or **Business Service**
- Put `LambdaQueryWrapper`, SQL, or pagination queries in Controller
- Duplicate the same DB query in multiple Controllers/BizServices — extract to `ServiceImpl` public methods

## Always

- Controller → `XxxBizService` only (HTTP + DTO return)
- BizService → orchestration, `@Transactional`, calls `XxxService` / other base services
- `XxxServiceImpl` extends `ServiceImpl<XxxMapper, XxxDomain>` — **all reusable DB methods live here**
- Mapper injected **only** in matching `ServiceImpl`

## Package layout (`senior-post-api/biz`)

- `controller.app` / `controller.admin`
- `service.biz`
- `service.base` (+ `*ServiceImpl`)
- `mapper`
- `model.domain`

## When touching existing code

If Controller or BizService already injects `Mapper`, **refactor** to the five-layer chain as part of the same task — do not add new cross-layer violations.

## Self-check before finishing

- [ ] No `Mapper` field in any Controller or `service.biz` class
- [ ] New queries added to `ServiceImpl`, not Controller
- [ ] Framework rules from skill still apply (`MyRequestContextHolder`, no manual `ApiResponse`, `PageQuery`/`PageData`, audit fields)
